2026-06-11 @ 14:30  Fix MariaDB stale lock crash loop

  Problem: MariaDB entered a crash loop with error 11 (EAGAIN) on
  aria_log_control and ibdata1.  fcntl locks are process-bound but on some
  container runtimes the replacement container starts before the previous
  process's OS resources are fully reaped, causing the new MariaDB to see a
  held lock and abort.

  Root cause: no graceful shutdown hook + no lock cleanup on restart.

  Modified file: helm/php-demo/templates/deployment.yaml
  - Added terminationGracePeriodSeconds: 60 to the pod spec so MariaDB
    receives SIGTERM with enough runway before SIGKILL.
  - Added initContainer mariadb-lock-cleanup (uses the same mariadb image)
    that removes aria_log_control, aria_log.00000001, multi-master.info and
    any *.pid files before the main container starts.  Removing
    aria_log_control is safe because all schema tables use InnoDB; MariaDB
    recreates the file and runs Aria crash recovery automatically.
  - Added lifecycle.preStop exec hook on the mariadb container:
    mariadb-admin shutdown flushes InnoDB/Aria and releases file locks
    cleanly before the kubelet sends SIGTERM.

  Immediate remediation (existing deployment):
    helm uninstall php-demo -n bpa-demo
    kubectl delete pvc php-demo-php-demo-mariadb-data -n bpa-demo
    ./scripts/deploy.sh

