2026-06-11 @ 12:42  Ingress class name configurable from .config

  Problem: ingress.className was hardcoded to "nginx" in values.yaml and
  never written into values.local.yaml by deploy.sh, making it impossible
  to target a different ingress controller (traefik, haproxy, alb, etc.)
  without editing the checked-in chart.

  Modified files:
  - .config.example
      Added INGRESS_CLASS_NAME variable (default "nginx") with a comment
      listing common alternatives.
  - scripts/deploy.sh
      Added className: "${INGRESS_CLASS_NAME}" to the ingress block written
      into values.local.yaml so the value flows from .config at deploy time.
  - helm/php-demo/values.yaml
      Set ingress.className default to "" (empty) with a comment directing
      operators to set INGRESS_CLASS_NAME in .config.
  - README.md
      Added INGRESS_CLASS_NAME to the .config example block; updated the
      Helm values table to show the empty default and its source.

